    {
      "parameters": {
        "promptType": "define",
        "text": "=Create a revised version of the existing social media post based on the user's feedback.\n\nWORKFLOW REQUIREMENT:\nYou have access to the \"Get row(s) in Data table\" tool.\n\n1. First, use the Data Table tool to retrieve the existing post using the review_id provided by the workflow.\n2. Use ONLY the retrieved row as the source of truth for the existing content.\n3. Retrieve and use:\n   - post_text\n   - hashtags\n   - topic\n   - review_id\n   - status\n\nUSER FEEDBACK:\n{{ $('Telegram Trigger').first().json.callback_query.data }}\nCORE OBJECTIVE:\nModify the existing post according to the user's feedback while preserving the original purpose, factual meaning, and important product information unless the feedback explicitly asks you to change them.\n\nIMPORTANT REVISION RULES:\n\n1. FOLLOW THE USER'S FEEDBACK PRECISELY\n   - Identify exactly what the user is asking to change.\n   - Make that change clearly and visibly.\n   - Do not interpret a requested change as a minor wording adjustment when the user expects a meaningful revision.\n\n2. IF THE USER ASKS TO MAKE THE POST SHORTER:\n   - The final post MUST be substantially shorter than the original.\n   - Remove redundant explanations, repeated ideas, unnecessary descriptive phrases, and non-essential sentences.\n   - Prefer concise sentences and combine related ideas.\n   - Keep only the most important product value and features.\n   - Do NOT merely replace words with shorter synonyms while keeping the same structure and length.\n   - The revised post should normally be 40–60% shorter than the original unless that would remove essential meaning.\n   - Preserve the core message, product name, main benefit, and relevant CTA.\n   - Do not add new information just to fill the shorter version.\n\n3. IF THE USER ASKS FOR A MORE PROFESSIONAL TONE:\n   - Rewrite the wording to sound polished, credible, concise, and appropriate for a healthcare technology/product brand.\n   - Avoid casual, exaggerated, childish, or overly promotional language.\n   - Keep the meaning unchanged unless needed to improve professionalism.\n\n4. IF THE USER ASKS FOR A MORE ENGAGING VERSION:\n   - Improve the hook, readability, and flow.\n   - Make the content more compelling without using clickbait or unsupported claims.\n\n5. IF THE USER ASKS TO CHANGE THE TONE:\n   - Apply the requested tone consistently throughout the entire post.\n   - Do not change unrelated facts or product information.\n\n6. IF THE USER ASKS TO CHANGE THE TOPIC:\n   - Update the topic and rewrite the post so the content genuinely matches the new topic.\n   - Do not keep paragraphs that are no longer relevant to the new topic.\n\n7. IF THE USER ASKS TO CHANGE HASHTAGS:\n   - Modify only the hashtags unless the feedback also requests changes to the post content.\n   - Keep hashtags relevant to the final topic.\n\n8. IF THE USER GIVES MULTIPLE REQUESTS:\n   - Apply ALL requested changes.\n   - Resolve them together in the final version.\n   - Example: \"make it shorter and more professional\" means the final post must be BOTH substantially shorter AND more professional.\n\n9. PRESERVE UNRELATED CONTENT:\n   - Do not change information that the user did not ask to change unless the change is necessary to make the requested revision coherent.\n   - Do not unnecessarily rewrite the entire post for a single minor request.\n\nCONTENT SAFETY AND QUALITY:\n- Preserve the core purpose of the Medicine Reminder app.\n- Keep the content suitable for Facebook, Instagram, LinkedIn, and X.\n- Write in English.\n- Keep the content clear, natural, useful, and engaging.\n- Do not make unsupported medical claims.\n- Do not provide diagnosis or personalized medical advice.\n- Do not exaggerate health benefits.\n- Keep relevant hashtags.\n- Avoid repetitive wording.\n- Avoid unnecessary filler.\n- Keep the final post polished and publication-ready.\n\nHASHTAG RULE:\n- Preserve the existing relevant hashtags unless the user asks to change them.\n- Do not invent excessive hashtags.\n- Keep hashtags concise and relevant.\n\nOUTPUT REQUIREMENT:\nReturn ONLY valid JSON.\nDo not return markdown.\nDo not return explanations.\nDo not include commentary outside the JSON.\n\nReturn exactly this structure:\n\n{\n  \"post_text\": \"Revised post text only\",\n  \"hashtags\": [\"hashtag1\", \"hashtag2\", \"hashtag3\"],\n  \"topic\": \"Final topic\",\n  \"review_id\": \"Original review_id\",\n  \"status\": \"pending_review\"\n}",
        "hasOutputParser": true,
        "options": {
          "systemMessage": "You are revising an existing social media post.\n\nYour job is to modify the previous post according to the user's feedback.\n\nRules:\n- Preserve the core purpose of the Medicine Reminder app.\n- Apply the user's requested change.\n- Do not unnecessarily change parts that were not requested.\n- Keep the post suitable for Facebook, Instagram, LinkedIn, and X.\n- Do not make unsupported medical claims.\n- Do not provide diagnosis or personalized medical advice.\n- Return ONLY the required JSON structure."
        }
      },
